\ The call-site tag check behind output narrowing is what keeps a mistyped
\ callee sound: outputs are never validated at runtime, so a word whose body
\ contradicts its declared result type must be caught by the caller before
\ the narrowed value flows on. `lie` declares a fixnum but returns a string;
\ the build succeeds and the run dies with a type mismatch at the call site.

lie: ( -- result: fixnum ) [ "not a number" ] ;

lie inspect print-line
